    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), so `OwnerDto` gains the getter/setter.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` that populates it via a new `telephoneDisplay(owner)` helper. The helper detects the country code (longest-prefix match against `61`/`1`, mirroring `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`), then emits `+<code> <national digits grouped in threes>`, e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. It returns the raw value unchanged for anything that isn't a recognised E.164 number.\n\nThe endpoint already maps the entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` in `RespondWithOwner`, so no wiring changes were needed. The `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` acceptance test (and the full suite) passes: `telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`.",
